# Written by `tauri_build::build()` on every compile — a build product, like
# `ui/src/lib/wasm/`. Committing it would mean a diff on every build and a
# merge conflict on none of them.
/gen/schemas/

# Generated by `cargo tauri android init`. Not ignored on purpose: the Gradle
# project is edited by hand (the manifest, the signing config, the launcher
# name), so it is source once it exists — the same call `cabas-relay/` makes
# about its Dockerfile. This line is here to say the choice was made.

# --- gen/android ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The project itself is committed: `AndroidManifest.xml`, the Gradle files and
# the signing config are edited by hand once a release build needs them, so
# they are source from the moment `android init` writes them. What is ignored
# below is everything the *build* puts back into that tree.
/gen/android/.gradle/
/gen/android/build/
/gen/android/app/build/
/gen/android/local.properties
# Written by the CLI on every build from `tauri.conf.json`'s version.
/gen/android/app/tauri.properties
# `WRY_ANDROID_KOTLIN_FILES_OUT_DIR` — regenerated from the Rust side.
/gen/android/app/src/main/java/**/generated/
